    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1363">

                <pb facs="1467" n="1453" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1453"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811F.504/10–1144</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 526</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panamá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-11">October 11,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received October 16.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my despatch
                    No. 372, September 19, 1944,<anchor n="66" xml:id="d1363-f1"/> regarding United
                    States Army labor policies in the Canal Zone and announcing the formation of a
                    special board for consideration of all civilian personnel matters, and to
                    forward attached a clipping<anchor n="67" xml:id="d1363-f2"/> from the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Star and Herald</hi> of October 6, 1944 announcing the
                    board’s decision regarding annual vacations of civilian employees of the Panama
                    Canal Department, United States Army.</p>
                <p>It will be noted that the new regulations authorize the granting of vacations on
                    a basis of equality as between United States citizen employees and non-United
                    States citizens whose base rates of pay, without counting overtime, are more
                    than 48 cents per hour, $100.00 per month, or $1,200.00 a year. The new
                    regulations cover all civilian employees of the Army in the Canal Zone and went
                    into effect October 1, to be continued for the duration of the actual
                    emergency.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. M. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
